      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 13th‑century Savelli palace, once a fortified residence, now houses the town’s historic center and echoes medieval architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albano_Laziale",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Beneath the Appian Way, the Catacombs of San Senatore were originally quarries before becoming a 2nd‑century Christian burial site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albano_Laziale",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Allied bombing on February 1 1944 devastated Albano’s historic center, striking the Poor Clares convent and Porta Pretoria Castra Albana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
